      "source": "import re\n\ndef slugify(title):\n    if not title:\n        return \"\"\n    title = title.lower()\n    title = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9\\-\\s]', '\\-', title)\n    title = re.sub(r'[-\\s]+', '-', title)\n    return title.rstrip('-')\n",
      "rationale": "The function first handles the empty string case. Then, it converts the input to lowercase and replaces all non-alphanumeric characters (except hyphens and spaces) with a single hyphen.  Next, it replaces multiple consecutive non-alphanumeric characters or spaces with a single hyphen. Finally, it strips any trailing hyphens.",
